Subject: [acs-r] Census API Back In Action: acs.R is once again fully
	functional
Message-ID: <87ppr22y9m.wl%eglenn@mit.edu>


Now that the federal government is back on its feet, the Census API is
serving up data again, and the acs.R package should work like it was
supposed to.

For example:

> acs.fetch(geo=geo.make(state=25), table.number="B01003")
ACS DATA: 
 2007 -- 2011 ;
  Estimates w/90% confidence intervals;
  for different intervals, see confint()
              B01003_001   
Massachusetts 6512227 +/- 0
> 

Hooray!

